      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking good, but I see two improvements we could do here.\n\n1) Frame blocks is not mandatory (by the BT spec) and when it is absent, it should be assumed to be 1, so if `frameb.has_value() \u003d\u003d false` we should act as it was actually set to 1.\n\n2) Another thing is that the `sduIntervalUs` calculation could be improved by multiplying the `frameDuration` (7500 or 10000) by `frameb`. Since if `frameb \u003e 1`, then there are multiple frames in a single SDU, then we can send the SDU `frameb` times less often because we are sending `frameb` number of (7500 or 10000 ms long) frames in one SDU. I hope that makes sense.",
